---
// Wording follows the CTIA Messaging Principles / 10DLC campaign checklist:
// program name and purpose, how to opt in, frequency, "Msg & data rates may
// apply", STOP and HELP, consent not a condition of purchase, carrier
// disclaimer, no sharing of mobile numbers, and a privacy policy link.
// SMS is not live (10DLC pending), so the page says so and describes the
// opt-in only as explicit consent, not a specific checkbox. When it
// launches: drop the Status section, put the program in the present tense,
// and name the actual opt-in step.
import LegalPage from "../components/legal/LegalPage.astro";
import { business } from "../data/business";

const programName = `${business.displayName} Notifications`;
---

<LegalPage
  title="SMS Terms"
  description={`Terms for text messages from ${business.displayName}: what we send, how often, and how to stop.`}
  path="/sms-terms"
  effectiveDate="October 12, 2026"
  noindex
>
  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>
    Text messaging is not active yet. We do not currently send text messages through this program,
    and nobody is signed up for it. These terms describe how it will work once it launches.
  </p>

  <h2>The program</h2>
  <p>
    When it launches, {programName} will send text messages to parents, guardians, and adult
    students who have opted in, about trial class bookings, class reminders, schedule changes and
    closures, and replies to questions you send us.
  </p>

  <h2>How you opt in</h2>
  <p>
    We will text you only after you give us your explicit consent to receive text messages from
    this program. We will ask for that consent separately, and we will not treat booking a class,
    filling out a form, or giving us your phone number as consent on its own. Consent to receive
    texts is never a condition of any purchase or enrollment.
  </p>

  <h2>Message frequency and cost</h2>
  <p>Message frequency will vary. Message and data rates may apply. Check your mobile plan for details.</p>

  <h2>Stopping and getting help</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to any message to stop receiving texts. We will send one confirmation and then no more.</li>
    <li>Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for help, or call us at <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Carriers</h2>
  <p>Wireless carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    We do not share your mobile number or text messaging consent with third parties or affiliates
    for their marketing purposes. See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle
    your information.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
